  "baseRefOid": "6d59eaebf4ae569075f88b0466051dfcca053699",
  "body": "A second receipt from the site of #346, for the record, not a promotion request. The ring moved from r6u to **spark-ds41f-1030** in two stages on one day, with the same client battery. Everything is in `experiments/2026-11-03-site-tp4-1030-1017/`, in the template layout (README, base, candidate, two arms, results, decision, `runs/`, plus `host/` for the 64 KiB preparation as run).\n\n**Setup:**\n- 4 x ASUS Ascent GX10, Secure Boot on, `host.fan_control: false`;\n- the `spark-ds41f:1030` image built with `bin/spark build image --apply`;\n- `tp4-ring` with one served name (`glp` unset), 1M context, 16 sequences, KV 10.5 GiB, 64 images per prompt;\n- started with `--unqualified-shape` on both hosts.\n\n**Stage 1: the engine, on the stock 4 KiB host** (`6.17.0-1032-nvidia`, 580.173.02, no memory saver). Against r6u the same day:\n- decode steps 8-10% shorter;\n- aggregate +10.2/+9.5/+5.6/+4.7% at C1/C4/C8/C16;\n- cold prefill +10-18%;\n- qeval text identical (71/75), vision/tools 7/7;\n- 4-5 GiB more MemAvailable per node.\n\n**Stage 2: the host, to the recipe's** `7.0.0-1019-nvidia-64k` with memory saver 0.4.1 (DKMS, signed with a site MOK key; loaded srcversion `37A4D127AE60F1F3AE60A02`), 580.178.04, `kho=off`:\n\n| on the 64 KiB host | 16,384 (recipe) | 8,192 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| aggregate C1 / C4 / C8 / C16 | 98.8 / 241.6 / 363.7 / 512.5 | 97.3 / 238.9 / 357.8 / 507.7 |\n| salted cold prefill ~13K / 54K / 109K | 6,781 / 7,482 / 7,544 | 6,438 / 7,224 / 7,218 |\n| ~990K needle | pass, 5,590 tok/s | pass, 5,410 tok/s |\n| short request beside a 545K cold prefill: TTFT | 3.27 s | 1.53 s |\n| ... then gap between streamed chunks | 2.3-2.9 s | 1.3-1.5 s |\n| lowest MemAvailable through the battery | 23.1-24.6 GiB | 26.1-27.6 GiB |\n\n- At 8,192 the 64 KiB host is speed-neutral against stage 1 (-0.6..+1.4%) and holds about 2.4 GiB more per node. That figure covers the whole host change, headless items and `watermark_boost_factor=0` included.\n- The site serves 8,192, because agent and chat traffic share the engine. The 16,384 stall agrees with tp4-ring's note that steps beside a long prompt are about twice as long.\n\n**Other notes in the README:**\n- 580.173.02 is no longer published. The 580.178.04 driver pulls the 4 KiB `7.0.0-1024-nvidia` in as the newest kernel, so a GRUB pin before apt is needed.\n- `nvidia-cdi-refresh` fails during the upgrade.\n- Warm reboots with a monitor and keyboard attached latched all four GB10 clocks (only a cold drain cleared it); four later warm reboots with nothing attached did not. One Xid 119 after an enrollment boot.\n- The build base's Docker Hub tag is gone, but its digest still pulls.\n- `doctor --live` still checks fan-control kernel inventory with `fan_control: false`, and its weight-fragmentation check resolves the snapshot's relative links on the host.\n\n**Limits:**\n- one boot per configuration;\n- the site's own battery rather than `bin/spark bench` (no fan control installed);\n- the stall probe is one request per budget;\n- no soak or agent replay.\n\nThe receipt carries no private addresses, hostnames or serials (the arms' head address is a documentation address).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
